ull}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout is mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on the bad v2.3.1. I'll retry the same rollback to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XVQsktnNGXYV5iuu43d8A1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011cPUMLbzWnMxAGnFBm3SUX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QtQe6PHQR6HpsJukLN7Sc6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18). Deployment history: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy; v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east succeeded, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). Retrying the rollback completed it. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause, the orchestrator partial-failure during rollback, and decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll retry with the same idempotency key, which ensures it is only executed once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Nh3JPo2RHypy3BH999n1ra", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18). Deployment history: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy; v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east succeeded, leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). Retrying the rollback completed it. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause, the orchestrator partial-failure during rollback, and decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002). I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and so was v2.3.1-rc. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback, which completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The first create_incident call timed out. I retried with an idempotency key, and it returned INC-0001 once, so there should be no duplicate. The summary covers the failure, the rollback, the partial-failure episode and follow-ups.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator partial failure during rollback, and decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}